WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.030
In 1963, Doctor Who
first aired on the BBC.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.590
Fifty years later, its anniversary episode
was screened at the same time on TV

3
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.530
and in cinemas around the world.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:20.090
In 2023, UK-qualifying films took 22.5
per cent of box office across 23 major

5
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.750
film markets.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.590
Britain sends its
stories out to the world.

7
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.130
But what has the world brought
to Britain's own culture?

8
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.790
New music?

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.130
New fashions?

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.470
In this mission, you'll see how
films and TV give Britain influence,

11
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.190
through attraction rather than force.

12
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.370
Then you'll explore how people who moved
here have shaped everyday British life.

13
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.710
Your mission: find out what people from
around the world have added to Britain's

14
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.730
own culture.
